Let us next consider the lens spaces. For p, q a pair of coprime integers, recall
that L(p, q) is given by surgery on S 3 along the unknot with surgery coefficient
−p/q . In the following corollary we include the possibilities L(0, 1) = S 1 × S 2
and L(1, q) = S 3 , q ∈ Z.

Corollary 4.2 ([17]) Let p, q be a pair of coprime integers. If q 6= 0 we let
(a1 , . . . , an−1 ) be a continued fraction expansion of −p/q . If q = 0, put n = 3
and a1 = a2 = 0. Then
                             τ (L(p, q)) = (∆D −1 )σ D −n GC00 ,                      (25)
